# EXAMPLE, focal variant (robodr-focal, systemd 245): NOT AVAILABLE here.
#
# The regular robodr package's 15-tpm-credentials.conf.example seals the
# robot's keys to the TPM with systemd encrypted credentials
# (LoadCredentialEncrypted=, systemd >= 250). systemd 245 has neither
# LoadCredentialEncrypted= nor systemd-creds, so on Ubuntu 20.04 the keys
# stay root-only files loaded by robodr-load-credential, and agentd reports
# each of them as "file" (not TPM-sealed, fallback: true) in status.json
# "key_protection"; "key_protection": {"require": "tpm2"} refuses to start.
# See docs/OPERATIONS.md, "Robot keys sealed to the TPM".
#
# There is nothing to install from this file.
